Container lifecycle changes: delete (create is planned, not built yet)
--delete stops a running container (confirmed, HA paused first so the watcher
does not race the confirmation), destroys it with 'pct destroy --purge
--destroy-unreferenced-disks' after a second confirmation (type the ID), then
removes it from the HA boot order, the NFS share state and the local mirror.
Backup archives, bind-mounted data and the standby host's ZFS copy are never
touched automatically.
